1
00:00:24,456 --> 00:00:25,816
Honey!

2
00:00:25,816 --> 00:00:27,275
Everyone, take a good look at this!

3
00:00:27,275 --> 00:00:29,669
This woman stole my husband!

4
00:00:30,001 --> 00:00:31,558
Investigate that girl's background.

5
00:00:32,034 --> 00:00:34,034
If she's chosen to
destroy my reputation...

6
00:00:34,232 --> 00:00:35,445
She will pay for it

7
00:00:36,204 --> 00:00:39,630
Isn't she the pregnant woman
who ruined your wedding?

8
00:00:39,631 --> 00:00:40,992
Hey! Wait, what?

9
00:00:41,427 --> 00:00:42,345
We've got her.

10
00:00:55,466 --> 00:00:56,614
And I suppose your twin...

11
00:00:57,322 --> 00:01:00,000
Also passed her baby-powder scent
on to you, huh?

12
00:01:02,812 --> 00:01:03,700
Ow!

13
00:01:04,961 --> 00:01:08,073
We stay together.

14
00:01:08,073 --> 00:01:08,809
So...

15
00:01:09,301 --> 00:01:11,301
We have the same smell.

16
00:01:15,966 --> 00:01:17,233
Then video-call her.

17
00:01:18,633 --> 00:01:20,100
Call your twin right now.

18
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,466
If she answers,

19
00:01:23,033 --> 00:01:24,100
I'll let you go.

20
00:01:29,466 --> 00:01:30,266
Call her!

21
00:01:33,433 --> 00:01:35,466
Ow!

22
00:01:35,466 --> 00:01:38,000
I think that won't happen.

23
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:38,800
My sister

24
00:01:38,866 --> 00:01:40,100
is probably asleep,

25
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:41,033
you know,

26
00:01:41,033 --> 00:01:41,966
because you forgot...

27
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:42,900
You forgot...

28
00:01:42,966 --> 00:01:43,766
She just had...

29
00:01:43,866 --> 00:01:44,666
a baby,

30
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:45,500
you know?

31
00:01:45,854 --> 00:01:47,854
She might be sleeping.

32
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:49,566
Stop making excuses.

33
00:01:52,614 --> 00:01:54,614
What happened?

34
00:01:56,489 --> 00:01:58,489
You gave birth,
and your belly shrank right away?

35
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:02,719
Bravo!

36
00:02:03,324 --> 00:02:04,869
What a medical miracle.

37
00:02:05,586 --> 00:02:06,878
Ow!

38
00:02:07,586 --> 00:02:10,395
Because the doctor is fantastic.

39
00:02:11,266 --> 00:02:13,233
Save your excuses for the police.

40
00:02:14,033 --> 00:02:15,900
Jaokha, call the police.

41
00:02:16,866 --> 00:02:17,666
Hey!

42
00:02:17,833 --> 00:02:19,566
It was just a wedding disruption.

43
00:02:19,766 --> 00:02:21,200
You have to call the police over that?

44
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:22,600
Hmph.

45
00:02:23,566 --> 00:02:24,600
You just admitted it.

46
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:26,666
You were just hired
to ruin my wedding, huh?

47
00:02:27,066 --> 00:02:28,566
My company's stock price dropped.

48
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,366
Investors pulled out.

49
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,766
The damages are incalculable.

50
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:34,833
And you still think it's no big deal?

51
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:36,666
Did you get through yet?

52
00:02:38,066 --> 00:02:38,866
I'm still trying.

53
00:02:39,066 --> 00:02:40,500
It keeps telling me
to press 1 and 2.

54
00:02:40,666 --> 00:02:41,566
It keep going in circles.

55
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,875
Then keep pressing them.

56
00:02:42,875 --> 00:02:43,375
Ow!

57
00:02:43,566 --> 00:02:44,866
The damn thing's bugged!

58
00:02:45,466 --> 00:02:46,266
Hey!

59
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:47,433
Are you okay?

60
00:03:00,503 --> 00:03:01,303
No.

61
00:03:02,054 --> 00:03:02,854
No, I can't.

62
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,233
I can't just leave.

63
00:03:06,466 --> 00:03:07,766
If I go back now,

64
00:03:08,966 --> 00:03:11,000
I won't get paid.

65
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:13,833
What should I do?

66
00:03:16,666 --> 00:03:18,046
Tell the manager

67
00:03:18,299 --> 00:03:19,906
to lock every exit.

68
00:03:20,412 --> 00:03:20,968
Right now!

69
00:03:21,474 --> 00:03:22,422
Okay.

70
00:03:37,366 --> 00:03:38,200
Did you find her?

71
00:03:38,666 --> 00:03:40,766
She's disappeared!
What are we gonna do now?

72
00:03:42,266 --> 00:03:43,002
It's fine.

73
00:03:44,418 --> 00:03:46,514
We'll check the security cameras
and see where she's hiding.

74
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,160
Jaokha.

75
00:04:03,424 --> 00:04:04,766
Can I borrow your lipstick?

76
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:06,740
What for?

77
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:07,300
Well...

78
00:04:09,033 --> 00:04:11,023
To make a murder scene

79
00:04:11,984 --> 00:04:14,100
and show that girl
who she's messing with.

80
00:04:16,466 --> 00:04:17,266
Here.

81
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:34,560
You guys go find the manager.

82
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:37,500
I'll look around here.

83
00:04:39,466 --> 00:04:41,766
Sure. Let's go, Jaokha.

84
00:04:50,076 --> 00:04:51,470
Let’s see

85
00:04:53,182 --> 00:04:56,723
Who can outlast the other in this game?

86
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:15,100
Ow!

87
00:06:15,766 --> 00:06:17,400
She probably gave up and went home.

88
00:06:19,466 --> 00:06:20,266
Right?

89
00:06:23,866 --> 00:06:24,666
Come on.

90
00:06:25,833 --> 00:06:27,266
Let's get back to work.

91
00:06:31,466 --> 00:06:32,266
My damn life...

92
00:06:38,266 --> 00:06:39,200
Playing hide-and-seek...

93
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:40,900
Having fun?

94
00:06:45,366 --> 00:06:46,166
You...

95
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:50,400
Hey!

96
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:51,800
Blood!

97
00:06:52,033 --> 00:06:53,033
This is your doing.

98
00:06:54,666 --> 00:06:56,033
You're a scammer,

99
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,466
a thief,

100
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,300
and a thug, too.

101
00:07:00,233 --> 00:07:01,700
You've got quite a rap sheet.

102
00:07:02,766 --> 00:07:04,766
I'm none of those things
you just called me.

103
00:07:08,466 --> 00:07:09,266
How about this?

104
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:12,066
I'll pay you back.

105
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:14,966
The money you stole?

106
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,366
That wouldn't even
cover my medical bills.

107
00:07:27,166 --> 00:07:27,966
What are you doing?

108
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:38,300
You...

109
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:48,133
I...

110
00:07:49,549 --> 00:07:51,450
I told you I didn't steal anything.

111
00:07:52,259 --> 00:07:52,804
That was...

112
00:07:53,158 --> 00:07:55,420
money the customers gave me as tips!

113
00:07:57,500 --> 00:07:58,400
Tips?

114
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:07,766
I'm not interested
in the money anymore.

115
00:08:09,166 --> 00:08:10,500
But I want to know...

116
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,900
Have you hidden anything else
from customers in your clothes?

117
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:22,000
Please let me go.

118
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:27,600
Take it off.

119
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:30,300
Huh?

120
00:08:31,033 --> 00:08:33,800
Take it off? Here?

121
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:38,467
Or should I call the police
to search you

122
00:08:39,731 --> 00:08:40,966
right here?

123
00:08:42,382 --> 00:08:43,066
Your choice.

124
00:08:49,066 --> 00:08:50,500
Please let me go.

125
00:08:54,233 --> 00:08:55,033
What are you doing?

126
00:08:58,100 --> 00:08:59,633
You're so flat.

127
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:05,966
So where did your baby come out, then?

128
00:09:08,066 --> 00:09:09,433
Tiger's mom.

129
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:15,166
Please let me go.

130
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:19,100
Scared?

131
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:22,662
Good.

132
00:09:23,673 --> 00:09:25,065
Remember this feeling.

133
00:09:26,633 --> 00:09:28,054
Because from now on,

134
00:09:28,914 --> 00:09:31,969
you'll pay me back until I'm satisfied.

135
00:09:40,166 --> 00:09:41,066
What are you doing?

136
00:09:42,066 --> 00:09:42,966
What are you doing?!

137
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,866
You recover pretty quickly.

138
00:09:48,033 --> 00:09:50,466
Your water broke in the morning,
and you're drinking at night.

139
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:57,000
My doctor is just that good.

140
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:02,458
A good doctor...

141
00:10:04,025 --> 00:10:05,084
Or was the pregnancy fake?

142
00:10:06,550 --> 00:10:09,351
I didn't expect you to show up
and get caught this soon.

143
00:10:10,918 --> 00:10:12,521
Who hired you?

144
00:10:15,233 --> 00:10:16,433
Nobody hired me.

145
00:10:18,366 --> 00:10:18,895
Really?

146
00:10:20,108 --> 00:10:22,994
But less than an hour after
you showed up at my wedding,

147
00:10:23,853 --> 00:10:26,418
embarrassing videos of me
were all over social media.

148
00:10:29,233 --> 00:10:30,900
What does that have to do with me?

149
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,200
It has everything to do with you.

150
00:10:33,866 --> 00:10:34,866
Those videos...

151
00:10:35,633 --> 00:10:37,066
Your people filmed them, didn't they?

152
00:10:37,766 --> 00:10:38,566
Huh?

153
00:10:39,366 --> 00:10:40,500
When you was crying,

154
00:10:41,566 --> 00:10:42,833
when your water broke,

155
00:10:43,366 --> 00:10:44,433
and when I fell.

156
00:10:45,366 --> 00:10:47,033
It was as if someone was waiting
to capture every moment.

157
00:10:48,866 --> 00:10:49,670
You...

158
00:10:50,226 --> 00:10:51,956
You think I staged all of this?

159
00:10:53,271 --> 00:10:56,368
Or are you going to say
it was a coincidence?

160
00:11:01,166 --> 00:11:04,063
Listen to me.

161
00:11:06,035 --> 00:11:07,316
I'll admit it.

162
00:11:11,066 --> 00:11:15,000
If I were really as good
at planning things as you say I am,

163
00:11:16,466 --> 00:11:18,766
I wouldn't have to come back
here and wait tables.

164
00:11:20,766 --> 00:11:21,353
Right?

165
00:11:23,830 --> 00:11:26,330
I'm telling you the truth.

166
00:11:28,049 --> 00:11:31,115
Someone really did hire me
to ruin your wedding.

167
00:11:33,846 --> 00:11:36,121
But those videos and all that stuff...

168
00:11:36,576 --> 00:11:38,456
I swear I know nothing about them.

169
00:11:39,766 --> 00:11:41,033
So you've admitted it.

170
00:11:43,066 --> 00:11:45,166
You were hired to ruin my wedding.

171
00:11:48,366 --> 00:11:49,156
In that case,

172
00:11:49,763 --> 00:11:51,943
you'll pay for all the damages from today.

173
00:11:52,904 --> 00:11:54,553
You will pay me back

174
00:11:55,109 --> 00:11:57,604
every single cent. Do you understand?

175
00:12:09,666 --> 00:12:10,902
You found her, huh?

176
00:12:10,902 --> 00:12:11,800
Yeah

177
00:12:12,566 --> 00:12:15,500
Took her long enough to come out.
I got eaten alive by mosquitoes.

178
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:18,366
What happened?

179
00:12:19,766 --> 00:12:21,666
What happened to your face, Mrs. Chat?

180
00:12:22,566 --> 00:12:24,600
Nant, why do you look like that?

181
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:29,433
Excuse me, Manager.

182
00:12:30,766 --> 00:12:32,400
What's the golden rule here?

183
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:36,566
At Rush Bar, the customer is king.

184
00:12:39,166 --> 00:12:41,433
The last employee got fired just
for stepping on a customer's foot.

185
00:12:42,766 --> 00:12:44,433
But I'm covered in blood.

186
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:53,502
Wait, I barely headbutted her, though.

187
00:12:53,502 --> 00:12:56,200
Look at my forehead.
There's not even a mark.

188
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:57,966
Not everyone has a hard head like you.

189
00:13:00,266 --> 00:13:01,962
Excuse me, Manager.

190
00:13:03,125 --> 00:13:04,513
If a staff member

191
00:13:05,019 --> 00:13:07,433
attacks a customer and
makes their head bleed like this,

192
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,866
is that against the rules?

193
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:12,200
Yes.

194
00:13:14,233 --> 00:13:15,700
And what happens

195
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:18,833
if they break the rules?

196
00:13:19,466 --> 00:13:20,266
They're fired.

197
00:13:25,166 --> 00:13:27,900
If she's fired,
do we still need the police?

198
00:13:28,266 --> 00:13:29,200
No, we don't.

199
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:31,400
Oh.

200
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:33,766
And blacklist this woman, too.

201
00:13:34,433 --> 00:13:36,266
I never want to see her here again.

202
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:45,062
Ai, Jaokha, let's go.

203
00:13:45,719 --> 00:13:46,666
I'm not having fun anymore.

204
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:47,900
Come on.

205
00:13:55,747 --> 00:13:56,635
But...

206
00:13:57,833 --> 00:14:00,296
I didn't do anything, sis.
I only barely headbutted her.

207
00:14:00,296 --> 00:14:02,100
If you didn't do anything,
why is her head bleeding?

208
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:04,800
You're lucky
she didn't have the police arrest you.

209
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:16,900
Do rich people think
they own the damn world?

210
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:19,400
Everyone just does
whatever they tell them to!

211
00:14:33,366 --> 00:14:34,166
Hey!

212
00:14:34,866 --> 00:14:35,700
Don't tell me...

213
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:37,366
It's out of gas?

214
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Why is this world so mean to me?

215
00:14:59,833 --> 00:15:00,681
You always blame everything else

216
00:15:01,187 --> 00:15:03,433
whenever you have a problem,

217
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:04,983
never yourself, don't you?

218
00:15:05,994 --> 00:15:07,381
Why don't you think about

219
00:15:07,935 --> 00:15:09,618
what you've done all this time

220
00:15:10,174 --> 00:15:11,643
to end up living like this?

221
00:15:14,424 --> 00:15:16,553
And is your motorbike broken down?

222
00:15:21,866 --> 00:15:23,839
Here. I'll help with the repair costs.

223
00:15:38,266 --> 00:15:39,066
Wow.

224
00:15:39,766 --> 00:15:41,400
Do you want money that badly?

225
00:15:41,966 --> 00:15:43,866
Mrs. Thitinant Inganant ******

226
00:15:45,266 --> 00:15:47,866
In life, we have plenty of choices.

227
00:15:49,166 --> 00:15:51,766
But you chose a path
that makes you worthless.

228
00:15:54,866 --> 00:15:55,700
Worthless?

229
00:15:57,033 --> 00:15:58,066
Yes, I'm poor.

230
00:15:58,700 --> 00:16:00,833
But I've never judged
someone's worth by their money.

231
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:03,200
You're the one

232
00:16:04,433 --> 00:16:06,666
who thinks money lets you
do whatever you want to anyone.

233
00:16:13,266 --> 00:16:14,178
Why?

234
00:16:14,684 --> 00:16:16,539
And what can
someone like you do about it?

235
00:16:26,166 --> 00:16:27,000
What are you doing?

236
00:16:29,266 --> 00:16:30,500
Kick your car, that's what!

237
00:16:32,833 --> 00:16:34,400
Stop! Are you crazy?!

238
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:35,300
No way!

239
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:37,566
I'm kicking it until I feel better!

240
00:16:38,166 --> 00:16:39,400
Chat, stop her.

241
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:40,433
That's your car.

242
00:16:40,633 --> 00:16:41,433
Why should I stop her?

243
00:16:41,766 --> 00:16:43,866
I'm not risking my neck
over some crazy girl.

244
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:49,100
Film it.

245
00:16:50,066 --> 00:16:50,966
The harder you kicks,

246
00:16:51,366 --> 00:16:52,766
the more expensive the damages will be.

247
00:16:53,366 --> 00:16:54,500
(Chat) This is satisfying.
(Nant) Keep filming!

248
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:55,951
Get a clear shot!

249
00:16:55,951 --> 00:16:56,466
Yeah.

250
00:16:56,633 --> 00:16:57,233
It's clear.

251
00:16:57,233 --> 00:16:58,150
Make sure you get it clearly!

252
00:16:58,150 --> 00:16:59,200
Yeah, crystal clear.

253
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:01,433
Go on!

254
00:17:01,433 --> 00:17:03,200
Is that all you can do?

255
00:17:04,366 --> 00:17:05,400
Fine, fine, fine!

256
00:17:08,461 --> 00:17:09,860
I'll call the insurance company.

257
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:14,751
Hello?

258
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:18,700
There's a dog attacking a car.

259
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:20,760
I'll send you the location.

260
00:17:23,187 --> 00:17:24,453
Tired already?

261
00:17:26,707 --> 00:17:28,707
Go on, do it.

262
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:35,766
The preliminary estimate
is 380,000 baht.

263
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:37,100
What?!

264
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:38,300
380,000?!

265
00:17:39,033 --> 00:17:39,833
Yes.

266
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:40,800
These are the details.

267
00:17:44,266 --> 00:17:46,627
All I did was kick the car,
and it's 380,000?

268
00:17:46,627 --> 00:17:47,521
Why?

269
00:17:47,521 --> 00:17:49,666
Why does the repair cost 380,000 baht?

270
00:17:52,033 --> 00:17:52,833
It's an imported car.

271
00:17:53,566 --> 00:17:54,566
The parts have to be imported.

272
00:17:55,233 --> 00:17:56,666
That's the standard rate.

273
00:17:58,433 --> 00:18:00,266
Stop complaining and sign it.

274
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:03,600
Sign here.

275
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,000
About the money.

276
00:18:24,566 --> 00:18:25,400
I don't have it.

277
00:18:26,900 --> 00:18:29,966
But I have something you want
even more than money.

278
00:18:32,100 --> 00:18:33,266
What nonsense
are you talking about now?

279
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,309
Well...

280
00:18:39,623 --> 00:18:41,233
It's about your former groom.

281
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:43,866
Didn't you know?

282
00:18:44,966 --> 00:18:46,500
He's not into women.

283
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,600
If that gets out to the press,

284
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:52,300
what will happen to your reputation?

285
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:59,077
And what do you think?

286
00:18:59,987 --> 00:19:02,690
If people find out Yong is gay,

287
00:19:03,347 --> 00:19:07,001
who do you think gets dragged harder,
you or me?

288
00:19:08,417 --> 00:19:10,427
A woman who got pregnant by a gay man..

289
00:19:11,742 --> 00:19:13,518
That's already an interesting headline.

290
00:19:14,529 --> 00:19:15,167
Don't you think?

291
00:19:19,100 --> 00:19:20,446
I figured as much.

292
00:19:20,446 --> 00:19:23,366
As if someone like you
would be bothered by this.

293
00:19:25,866 --> 00:19:28,033
But I've got something even better.

294
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:40,256
Ai, Jaokha, you can go back first.

295
00:19:40,762 --> 00:19:42,048
I need to settle something
with this girl.

296
00:19:43,514 --> 00:19:46,033
About you.
I'll get back to you later.

297
00:19:46,566 --> 00:19:47,366
Yes, ma'am.

298
00:20:08,066 --> 00:20:08,866
Ow!

299
00:20:09,033 --> 00:20:10,233
What the hell are you doing?

300
00:20:14,833 --> 00:20:15,633
All done.

301
00:20:16,566 --> 00:20:17,966
Tomorrow's headline:

302
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:19,500
CEO

303
00:20:20,966 --> 00:20:23,555
caught having an affair with...

304
00:20:24,516 --> 00:20:25,935
her own groom's girl.

305
00:20:28,866 --> 00:20:29,666
Oh.

306
00:20:32,066 --> 00:20:33,500
You'll be even more famous now.

307
00:20:38,766 --> 00:20:39,566
Sigh...

308
00:20:39,866 --> 00:20:42,100
You think this lousy
deepfake video will work?

309
00:20:42,866 --> 00:20:44,700
Now you'll face even more charges

310
00:20:45,266 --> 00:20:46,466
for fabricating false information

311
00:20:47,066 --> 00:20:48,233
and slandering me.

312
00:20:50,166 --> 00:20:51,700
You'll be going to prison
for a long time.

313
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:56,816
I figured as much.

314
00:20:56,816 --> 00:20:59,400
As if someone like you
would be bothered by this.

315
00:21:03,700 --> 00:21:05,400
Let's check out the real deal, then.

316
00:21:12,066 --> 00:21:12,866
I've had enough!

317
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:15,966
Please, just let me go.

318
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:18,366
Your men beat me half to death

319
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:20,033
or running away from the wedding.

320
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:23,433
What's this video?

321
00:21:23,900 --> 00:21:24,700
Oh?

322
00:21:24,833 --> 00:21:28,300
Oh, just the video of you getting
your ex-groom beaten up.

323
00:21:28,833 --> 00:21:29,700
Don't you remember?

324
00:21:30,966 --> 00:21:31,766
Ooh.

325
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,400
If this gets out...

326
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:37,266
Oh, what if this video gets
into the hands of the press?

327
00:21:39,266 --> 00:21:41,233
I don't even want to think about it.

328
00:21:47,716 --> 00:21:51,182
No, no, no.

329
00:21:52,633 --> 00:21:53,833
What exactly do you want?

330
00:21:55,033 --> 00:21:56,600
This is so cute.

331
00:21:57,833 --> 00:22:00,233
Now we're talking.

332
00:22:03,666 --> 00:22:07,300
First, you have to waive
the car repair costs.

333
00:22:12,066 --> 00:22:14,315
In exchange,
you have to delete that video.

334
00:22:14,315 --> 00:22:15,468
I'm not done yet.

335
00:22:16,176 --> 00:22:19,153
Second, you have to hire me

336
00:22:20,566 --> 00:22:24,174
as your personal secretary intern

337
00:22:24,882 --> 00:22:28,385
for three months, at double the salary.

338
00:22:30,033 --> 00:22:33,066
In your dreams!
Why would I let you work by my side?

339
00:22:34,200 --> 00:22:35,466
Suit yourself.

340
00:22:37,666 --> 00:22:41,566
But your reputation is in my hands now.

341
00:22:45,700 --> 00:22:46,700
How about now?

342
00:22:51,566 --> 00:22:53,300
Go ahead, scream.
Scream all you want.

343
00:22:57,700 --> 00:22:59,875
Just remember this.

344
00:23:00,482 --> 00:23:03,633
Working at my company
will be hell for you.

345
00:23:05,600 --> 00:23:07,352
Hell with double the salary?

346
00:23:08,110 --> 00:23:10,524
Totally worth it.

347
00:23:16,033 --> 00:23:17,033
Seven sharp.

348
00:23:17,700 --> 00:23:19,700
Don't be late, not even by a second.

349
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:22,100
You got it.

350
00:23:24,100 --> 00:23:26,600
My name is Thitinant.

351
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:29,266
You can just call me Nant.

352
00:23:31,266 --> 00:23:32,266
See you tomorrow.

353
00:23:33,879 --> 00:23:35,879
See you, baby.

354
00:23:47,966 --> 00:23:49,800
I can't believe someone
could be this shameless.

355
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:54,833
Get a hold of yourself.

356
00:23:55,033 --> 00:23:55,833
Theerachat.

357
00:24:31,366 --> 00:24:32,300
Good morning.

358
00:24:33,366 --> 00:24:34,166
Yeah.

359
00:24:34,166 --> 00:24:36,109
Boss Chat says you have to wait here.

360
00:24:36,109 --> 00:24:37,296
Don't get up.

361
00:24:37,296 --> 00:24:38,357
Don't make any noise.

362
00:24:38,357 --> 00:24:41,100
And absolutely do not go near
her office unless you're called in.

363
00:24:41,566 --> 00:24:42,366
Yes.

364
00:25:19,166 --> 00:25:19,966
Hey, you.

365
00:25:20,366 --> 00:25:21,600
You're Thitinant, right?

366
00:25:22,666 --> 00:25:23,466
Hey, you!

367
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:25,000
Hey!

368
00:25:25,233 --> 00:25:26,233
You're Thitinant, right?

369
00:25:43,966 --> 00:25:45,992
Good morning, I'm Nant.

370
00:25:46,801 --> 00:25:49,100
Boss Chat told me
to come here as an intern.

371
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:50,100
Yes.

372
00:25:50,707 --> 00:25:51,486
I know.

373
00:25:52,750 --> 00:25:54,267
I've been seeing your face all night.

374
00:25:57,500 --> 00:25:58,485
Yes.

375
00:25:59,092 --> 00:26:00,197
My name is Hanna.

376
00:26:00,450 --> 00:26:01,506
I'm Boss Chat's secretary.

377
00:26:02,618 --> 00:26:05,086
You can call me Hanna.

378
00:26:05,700 --> 00:26:06,500
Okay.

379
00:26:07,166 --> 00:26:07,966
Sure.

380
00:26:08,433 --> 00:26:09,466
Hannah.

381
00:26:10,800 --> 00:26:12,066
Wait here for now.

382
00:26:14,233 --> 00:26:15,066
Don't get up.

383
00:26:15,966 --> 00:26:16,800
Don't make any noise.

384
00:26:18,500 --> 00:26:20,300
Don't go anywhere near her office.

385
00:26:21,233 --> 00:26:22,366
Not unless you're told to.

386
00:26:23,966 --> 00:26:24,766
Yes.

387
00:26:25,166 --> 00:26:26,900
Boss Chat asked me to pass that along.

388
00:26:27,866 --> 00:26:28,566
Yes.

389
00:26:28,566 --> 00:26:29,366
Understood.

390
00:26:30,233 --> 00:26:31,033
Yes.

391
00:26:58,433 --> 00:26:59,400
Nant?

392
00:27:00,400 --> 00:27:01,200
Nant.

393
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:04,400
Nant?

394
00:27:19,500 --> 00:27:20,300
Good morning.

395
00:27:29,366 --> 00:27:31,100
Has Boss Chat called me in yet?

396
00:27:32,433 --> 00:27:34,100
The boss is busy right now.

397
00:27:35,833 --> 00:27:37,700
She has to sort out the mess
from yesterday's wedding.

398
00:27:38,633 --> 00:27:41,600
Who knew someone
could cause such a huge mess?

399
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:44,700
Keep waiting, okay?

400
00:27:48,466 --> 00:27:49,266
Yes.

401
00:27:53,166 --> 00:27:54,900
Waiting here is no problem at all.

402
00:28:23,566 --> 00:28:24,586
Boss Chat?

403
00:28:25,041 --> 00:28:27,262
That girl has been
waiting for five hours.

404
00:28:27,262 --> 00:28:28,633
Should I ask her to come in?

405
00:28:30,266 --> 00:28:31,766
Feeling sorry for her, Secretary Han?

406
00:28:34,433 --> 00:28:35,233
No, boss.

407
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:38,200
Just let her keep waiting.

408
00:28:38,633 --> 00:28:39,700
If she can handle it, let her.

409
00:28:39,966 --> 00:28:42,566
If not, she'll give up
and leave on her own.

410
00:28:43,700 --> 00:28:44,500
Yes, boss.

411
00:28:44,833 --> 00:28:45,666
And one more thing.

412
00:28:46,400 --> 00:28:48,233
I don't want anything
to do with that girl.

413
00:28:49,200 --> 00:28:50,833
Go get Mr. Wichai for me.

414
00:28:51,766 --> 00:28:52,800
Understood, boss.

415
00:28:57,366 --> 00:28:57,866
Um...

416
00:28:59,079 --> 00:29:00,731
Has Boss Chat called me in yet?

417
00:29:03,566 --> 00:29:04,778
Boss Chat is busy.

418
00:29:05,536 --> 00:29:06,279
So...

419
00:29:07,290 --> 00:29:08,093
Sit.

420
00:29:08,093 --> 00:29:08,593
And wait.

421
00:29:09,503 --> 00:29:10,705
For now, okay?

422
00:29:17,166 --> 00:29:18,033
Understood.

423
00:29:38,033 --> 00:29:38,833
Close the door!

424
00:29:41,700 --> 00:29:42,500
Close it!

425
00:30:06,366 --> 00:30:07,266
It's already three in the afternoon.

426
00:30:10,500 --> 00:30:11,300
I'm starving.

427
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:27,800
Here.

428
00:30:29,233 --> 00:30:30,033
Eat up.

429
00:30:35,966 --> 00:30:36,766
Thank you.

430
00:30:39,900 --> 00:30:41,766
And don't leave the wrapper
lying around when you're done.

431
00:30:42,833 --> 00:30:43,633
Thank you.

432
00:30:44,400 --> 00:30:47,166
I'd be in real trouble

433
00:30:47,900 --> 00:30:49,100
without you, Hanna

434
00:30:51,366 --> 00:30:54,100
Eat, then sit quietly.
Don't go anywhere.

435
00:31:31,966 --> 00:31:35,700
Wait a second, Nant. You're interning
at Mrs. Chat's company?

436
00:31:37,366 --> 00:31:38,166
Yeah.

437
00:31:39,966 --> 00:31:41,433
You've lost your mind, Nant.

438
00:31:41,966 --> 00:31:43,066
You're practically asking to die.

439
00:31:44,966 --> 00:31:46,366
Haven't you heard?

440
00:31:47,633 --> 00:31:49,166
The most dangerous place

441
00:31:49,666 --> 00:31:51,100
is the safest place.

442
00:31:51,633 --> 00:31:52,433
Sure, whatever you say.

443
00:31:53,033 --> 00:31:55,800
You'll be lucky to make it
out of there in one piece today.

444
00:31:59,600 --> 00:32:00,566
Just talking about her
makes my blood boil.

445
00:32:01,033 --> 00:32:02,000
She's so cruel!

446
00:32:02,400 --> 00:32:05,066
She left me
waiting outside her office all day.

447
00:32:06,366 --> 00:32:07,166
I needed to pee.

448
00:32:07,400 --> 00:32:08,200
I was starving, too.

449
00:32:08,800 --> 00:32:10,300
I was too scared
to get up and go anywhere.

450
00:32:10,666 --> 00:32:11,766
I was afraid
she'd call for me while I was gone.

451
00:32:16,200 --> 00:32:17,600
By the way, what about your parents?

452
00:32:17,800 --> 00:32:19,021
Didn't they scold you at all?

453
00:32:19,021 --> 00:32:19,633
Hmm.

454
00:32:20,666 --> 00:32:21,466
No, they didn't.

455
00:32:22,200 --> 00:32:23,000
Really?

456
00:32:26,166 --> 00:32:29,166
So she didn't tell your family
about my fake pregnancy prank?

457
00:32:29,666 --> 00:32:31,227
I guess she didn't want
to make a scene.

458
00:32:32,036 --> 00:32:34,600
So she just let my Pa take all
the blame at the press conference.

459
00:32:35,433 --> 00:32:37,633
After causing such a huge mess,

460
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:40,633
Won't your parents
cut you out of the will?

461
00:32:40,833 --> 00:32:41,769
I got chewed out pretty badly.

462
00:32:41,769 --> 00:32:43,366
But don't forget,

463
00:32:43,366 --> 00:32:45,915
I'm the only son in the family.

464
00:32:46,724 --> 00:32:49,466
They just put on a show of being mad.
They'll go easy on me in the end.

465
00:32:49,833 --> 00:32:50,333
Yeah.

466
00:32:50,990 --> 00:32:53,000
At least your family
didn't recognize Nant.

467
00:32:53,866 --> 00:32:54,366
Right.

468
00:32:54,770 --> 00:32:56,404
But I'm still stressed out.

469
00:32:56,900 --> 00:32:57,559
Well...

470
00:32:58,216 --> 00:32:59,966
My mom's trying to find me
another wife again.

471
00:33:00,300 --> 00:33:00,994
Oh, come on.

472
00:33:01,752 --> 00:33:04,600
Just tell her you're not into women.

473
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:06,000
I don't have the guts.

474
00:33:06,633 --> 00:33:10,900
Oh, then just put up with it
and stop complaining, Your Highness.

475
00:33:11,633 --> 00:33:12,433
And...

476
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:14,000
Nant.

477
00:33:14,800 --> 00:33:16,366
Besides watching out for Mrs. Chat,

478
00:33:16,600 --> 00:33:18,666
don't forget your ex, Mind.

479
00:33:18,800 --> 00:33:20,300
She works at this company, too.

480
00:33:22,433 --> 00:33:23,233
I know.

481
00:33:24,366 --> 00:33:26,600
But she's in the design department.

482
00:33:26,833 --> 00:33:27,866
I probably won't run into her.

483
00:33:28,300 --> 00:33:29,100
Oh.

484
00:33:29,466 --> 00:33:30,566
Yeah, right!

485
00:33:31,100 --> 00:33:32,233
You broke up ages ago.

486
00:33:32,600 --> 00:33:34,500
When are you going to
stop checking her stories?

487
00:33:35,166 --> 00:33:36,066
She cheated on you

488
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:37,900
and abused you.

489
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:41,233
It took everything to
get you away from her.

490
00:33:41,433 --> 00:33:43,100
We almost had to
take you to get a curse lifted.

491
00:33:44,366 --> 00:33:45,600
Stop talking about her already.

492
00:33:46,700 --> 00:33:48,066
I'm not falling for her again.

493
00:33:58,200 --> 00:33:59,135
Hello?

494
00:34:00,551 --> 00:34:01,296
Yes.

495
00:34:01,903 --> 00:34:02,932
I'm on my way.

496
00:34:03,791 --> 00:34:05,308
I'll be there in an hour.

497
00:34:05,864 --> 00:34:07,620
Okay, see you then.

498
00:34:12,033 --> 00:34:12,900
I'm heading out.

499
00:34:14,100 --> 00:34:17,033
I've got a fake-girlfriend gig today.

500
00:34:23,033 --> 00:34:23,833
See you.

501
00:34:25,033 --> 00:34:25,533
Yeah.

502
00:34:25,533 --> 00:34:26,100
See you.

503
00:34:26,500 --> 00:34:28,939
Get paid and come straight home.
Don't go drinking afterward.

504
00:34:28,939 --> 00:34:31,033
You have to go to war
with Mrs. Chat first thing tomorrow.

505
00:34:31,866 --> 00:34:34,033
Sure thing. Bye!

506
00:34:34,766 --> 00:34:35,566
Bye.

507
00:34:47,233 --> 00:34:48,912
Oh! Good morning, Boss Chat!

508
00:34:49,569 --> 00:34:51,823
I've been here since six-thirty.

509
00:35:33,766 --> 00:35:34,700
Boss Chat?

510
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:38,466
What is that girl up to?

511
00:35:40,500 --> 00:35:42,166
I'm not quite sure either.

512
00:35:42,600 --> 00:35:43,900
Would you like me to go check?

513
00:35:45,374 --> 00:35:46,515
Yeah.

514
00:35:48,433 --> 00:35:50,433
I'll go take a look.

515
00:35:59,066 --> 00:35:59,866
Wow.

516
00:36:01,700 --> 00:36:02,866
She's folding those so fast.

517
00:36:03,500 --> 00:36:04,300
What are you doing?

518
00:36:05,800 --> 00:36:06,666
This is an office,

519
00:36:06,966 --> 00:36:07,833
not a temple fair.

520
00:36:09,100 --> 00:36:09,900
Oh.

521
00:36:10,766 --> 00:36:11,566
Um...

522
00:36:11,900 --> 00:36:13,200
I knew the boss

523
00:36:13,400 --> 00:36:15,266
wouldn't have time to call me in,

524
00:36:16,466 --> 00:36:19,233
so I took an order to fold money
cones for a ceremony.

525
00:36:19,900 --> 00:36:20,700
Hmph.

526
00:36:21,700 --> 00:36:24,566
My time is money, after all.

527
00:36:30,233 --> 00:36:31,400
May I take a look?

528
00:36:35,833 --> 00:36:37,327
You'd better put those away.

529
00:36:37,327 --> 00:36:39,500
The boss will scold you
if she sees them.

530
00:36:42,833 --> 00:36:44,500
Then she can come out
and scold me herself.

531
00:36:45,600 --> 00:36:47,566
Instead of hiding behind the blinds.

532
00:36:50,900 --> 00:36:51,700
Hello?

533
00:36:52,366 --> 00:36:53,166
Yeah, yeah.

534
00:37:00,200 --> 00:37:01,366
You'd better put those away.

535
00:37:09,266 --> 00:37:09,918
Boss?

536
00:37:09,918 --> 00:37:10,666
Hmm?

537
00:37:10,900 --> 00:37:12,200
Money cones for a ceremony.

538
00:37:14,366 --> 00:37:15,166
Unbelievable.

539
00:37:15,900 --> 00:37:16,800
Absolutely amazing.

540
00:37:17,600 --> 00:37:18,766
I can't believe someone
like her exists.

541
00:37:25,966 --> 00:37:26,866
Secretary Han.

542
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:28,565
Yes, boss?

543
00:37:28,565 --> 00:37:30,359
Take these reports from
the past three years

544
00:37:30,713 --> 00:37:32,033
and have that girl sort them out.

545
00:37:32,700 --> 00:37:33,607
All of these?

546
00:37:33,910 --> 00:37:37,066
It would take me a whole week
to organize them, boss.

547
00:37:37,500 --> 00:37:38,776
Get them done today.

548
00:37:39,534 --> 00:37:41,500
If she can't do that,
don't bother coming in tomorrow.

549
00:37:42,300 --> 00:37:43,233
Understood, boss.

550
00:37:54,833 --> 00:37:56,433
So your time is money, huh?

551
00:37:57,366 --> 00:37:59,633
I'll teach you what
the real world is like.

552
00:38:00,266 --> 00:38:01,233
You little troublemaker.

553
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:13,669
Sign it.

554
00:38:14,377 --> 00:38:15,566
I don't have all day.

555
00:38:18,833 --> 00:38:19,633
Um...

556
00:38:21,033 --> 00:38:21,833
The language...

557
00:38:24,033 --> 00:38:26,500
The company is expanding into China,

558
00:38:27,166 --> 00:38:29,200
so the assistant's contract
is in Chinese, too.

559
00:38:30,666 --> 00:38:31,466
What?

560
00:38:32,100 --> 00:38:33,000
Can't read it?

561
00:38:42,666 --> 00:38:44,566
[Clause 1: Employee]

562
00:38:45,700 --> 00:38:47,666
Must follow all orders
from the employer.

563
00:38:49,866 --> 00:38:50,792
[Clause 5]

564
00:38:50,792 --> 00:38:51,856
Clause five.

565
00:38:52,159 --> 00:38:53,588
Double salary, as agreed.

566
00:38:53,588 --> 00:38:57,136
Am I your personal assistant
or your general servant?

567
00:38:57,829 --> 00:39:00,100
Since when do waiters speak
such fluent Chinese?

568
00:39:00,633 --> 00:39:03,866
Well, Chinese guests
give big tips, boss.

569
00:39:05,500 --> 00:39:06,300
Oh.

570
00:39:06,666 --> 00:39:07,766
I almost forgot.

571
00:39:08,866 --> 00:39:09,666
Here you go.

572
00:39:10,033 --> 00:39:12,600
I've been folding these
for you all day, boss.

573
00:39:12,833 --> 00:39:13,633
These ones.

574
00:39:13,666 --> 00:39:15,800
You can use them
at your next wedding, boss.

575
00:39:16,200 --> 00:39:18,300
Maybe it'll keep it
from falling apart this time.

576
00:39:19,300 --> 00:39:20,766
Save them for your own funeral.

577
00:39:21,100 --> 00:39:22,800
Oh, I can't do that, boss.

578
00:39:23,366 --> 00:39:25,100
This color is considered lucky.

579
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:26,917
If...

580
00:39:26,917 --> 00:39:27,417
Um...

581
00:39:28,100 --> 00:39:31,033
I think I'd better take
Nant to get started on her work.

582
00:39:31,433 --> 00:39:32,233
Start now.

583
00:39:33,833 --> 00:39:35,866
Then let's get going. Come on.

584
00:39:37,233 --> 00:39:38,033
Get up.

585
00:39:39,366 --> 00:39:40,833
Aren't you taking the contract?

586
00:39:44,666 --> 00:39:46,433
I'll take care of it, boss.

587
00:39:56,566 --> 00:39:58,300
Save them for your own funeral.

588
00:39:59,033 --> 00:39:59,833
Thitinant!

589
00:40:08,666 --> 00:40:09,466
Annoying.

590
00:40:18,566 --> 00:40:19,566
Nant...

591
00:40:23,900 --> 00:40:26,066
I've worked with the boss for years,

592
00:40:26,466 --> 00:40:29,666
I've never seen anyone annoy the boss
every five minutes like you do.

593
00:40:31,233 --> 00:40:33,300
But the boss always picks on me first.

594
00:40:35,066 --> 00:40:36,633
You have to be calm.

595
00:40:37,500 --> 00:40:38,866
Don't cause trouble for the boss.

596
00:40:39,433 --> 00:40:41,300
I don't want to be
cleaning up a body at work.

597
00:40:45,233 --> 00:40:46,033
Okay.

598
00:40:47,100 --> 00:40:47,900
Let's go.

599
00:40:48,300 --> 00:40:49,200
It's your first day.

600
00:40:49,766 --> 00:40:51,800
Don't give me any more headaches, okay?

601
00:40:55,633 --> 00:40:57,066
Understood, Hanna.

602
00:41:08,033 --> 00:41:08,833
It the numbers

603
00:41:08,833 --> 00:41:10,066
don't align with our last

604
00:41:10,200 --> 00:41:10,666
quarter

605
00:41:10,666 --> 00:41:11,466
projection

606
00:41:11,466 --> 00:41:12,666
I'm afraid we cannot

607
00:41:14,600 --> 00:41:16,666
[If we can't resolve this issue,]

608
00:41:16,666 --> 00:41:18,233
[there's no point in
continuing this discussion.]

609
00:41:26,233 --> 00:41:28,500
Have you finished entering
the sales figures?

610
00:41:31,633 --> 00:41:34,100
Did Mom ask you to get
the documents for tomorrow's meeting?

611
00:41:34,466 --> 00:41:37,400
Yes. Um, Chat, I have a question.

612
00:41:38,066 --> 00:41:39,509
Is it work-related?

613
00:41:40,116 --> 00:41:42,950
If not, wait until I'm done working.

614
00:41:44,770 --> 00:41:45,566
Go ahead.

615
00:41:47,700 --> 00:41:48,500
Sure.

616
00:41:51,766 --> 00:41:54,600
This is the quarterly
comparison dashboard.

617
00:41:55,100 --> 00:41:58,966
The highlighted points here
show unusual costs.

618
00:41:59,700 --> 00:42:02,966
And over here, I've translated
the comments from our Chinese clients.

619
00:42:18,300 --> 00:42:20,750
It's decent enough

620
00:42:21,104 --> 00:42:22,033
for an intern.

621
00:42:24,100 --> 00:42:26,866
Wait, you did all this yourself?

622
00:42:28,500 --> 00:42:29,300
Yes.

623
00:42:30,066 --> 00:42:32,400
Wow, this is really good, Chat!

624
00:42:32,600 --> 00:42:34,433
Why'd you say it's just decent?

625
00:42:35,266 --> 00:42:37,866
Oh, if you're done,
you can leave now, Chom.

626
00:42:38,068 --> 00:42:38,568
Go on.

627
00:42:38,568 --> 00:42:39,266
What?

628
00:42:39,700 --> 00:42:40,500
Okay.

629
00:42:40,800 --> 00:42:41,600
Fine, I'll go.

630
00:42:48,800 --> 00:42:49,600
Close the door.

631
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:50,800
Okay.

632
00:42:54,800 --> 00:42:57,266
Your sister is pretty cute.

633
00:42:59,266 --> 00:43:00,600
But the boss is even cuter.

634
00:43:06,466 --> 00:43:07,633
Why are you smiling, Boss?

635
00:43:10,900 --> 00:43:12,233
Get back to work.

636
00:43:12,766 --> 00:43:13,566
Go!

637
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:14,800
Yes, boss.

638
00:43:15,633 --> 00:43:18,033
But can I have my iPad back, please?

639
00:44:05,866 --> 00:44:06,866
Thitinant.

640
00:44:18,900 --> 00:44:20,400
Thitinant Inganan!

641
00:44:23,666 --> 00:44:25,666
Stop making all that annoying noise!

642
00:44:26,666 --> 00:44:27,467
And another thing,

643
00:44:28,428 --> 00:44:30,600
could you dress more appropriately
for the workplace?

644
00:44:31,566 --> 00:44:33,166
This is an office, not your home.

645
00:44:33,700 --> 00:44:36,200
But this is
my university uniform, Boss.

646
00:44:36,900 --> 00:44:39,033
It's just a little disheveled.

647
00:44:40,500 --> 00:44:41,300
But...

648
00:44:41,966 --> 00:44:43,566
It's perfectly clean, Boss.

649
00:44:46,400 --> 00:44:47,300
And it smells really nice, too.

650
00:44:47,966 --> 00:44:49,433
Want to smell it, Boss?

651
00:44:51,366 --> 00:44:52,700
Cleanliness and appropriateness

652
00:44:53,400 --> 00:44:54,400
are two different things.

653
00:44:55,466 --> 00:44:57,700
Dress more professionally tomorrow.

654
00:44:57,866 --> 00:44:59,166
Okay, okay.

655
00:44:59,566 --> 00:45:03,400
I'll dress extra nicely tomorrow, Boss.

656
00:45:05,633 --> 00:45:06,238
Good.

657
00:45:07,451 --> 00:45:09,481
Use the money you
earn from your dirty work

658
00:45:10,088 --> 00:45:12,558
to buy yourself some expensive clothes.

659
00:45:17,033 --> 00:45:19,233
So you judge people
by what they wear, Boss?

660
00:45:20,600 --> 00:45:21,966
Be careful. You might get fooled.

661
00:45:23,000 --> 00:45:24,700
Plenty of people who dress expensively

662
00:45:25,900 --> 00:45:27,700
behave terribly.

663
00:45:29,566 --> 00:45:30,666
Are you talking about me?

664
00:45:31,366 --> 00:45:33,666
Is your thousand-baht bill
as big as a house, Boss?

665
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:36,166
I'm just telling the truth.

666
00:45:37,100 --> 00:45:38,500
Do you think being rich

667
00:45:38,966 --> 00:45:40,066
puts you above everyone else

668
00:45:40,466 --> 00:45:42,300
and gives you the right to judge them?

669
00:45:44,000 --> 00:45:45,800
I've never thought I'm above anyone.

670
00:45:46,800 --> 00:45:49,166
But I've never lowered
my standards,either.

671
00:45:50,800 --> 00:45:52,124
Then how about a bet?

672
00:45:53,186 --> 00:45:54,000
One day,

673
00:45:54,708 --> 00:45:56,368
those high standards of yours

674
00:45:57,126 --> 00:45:59,200
will come down for this girl.

675
00:46:00,700 --> 00:46:02,433
You'll end up begging to
get into bed with me.

676
00:46:03,433 --> 00:46:04,233
You're so full of yourself.

677
00:46:05,166 --> 00:46:06,466
You think someone like you

678
00:46:06,900 --> 00:46:08,766
could make me beg to sleep with you?

679
00:46:09,400 --> 00:46:11,766
Here's the deal. If you fall for me,

680
00:46:12,566 --> 00:46:14,466
you'll have to become
my servant instead.

681
00:46:15,033 --> 00:46:15,833
Do you dare?

682
00:46:20,366 --> 00:46:21,384
You're awfully confident, aren't you?

683
00:46:22,294 --> 00:46:22,794
Remember this.

684
00:46:23,502 --> 00:46:26,321
I'd never stoop so low as
to waste my time on a girl like you.

685
00:46:29,300 --> 00:46:30,627
Get ready to eat your words.

686
00:46:31,840 --> 00:46:33,362
Because this girl right here

687
00:46:33,766 --> 00:46:35,130
will make you fall for her

688
00:46:35,433 --> 00:46:37,060
so hard you won't be able to escape.
Just you wait.

689
00:46:55,266 --> 00:46:57,766
In your dreams. Never gonna happen.

690
00:47:16,866 --> 00:47:18,766
Here's the coffee you like, Boss.

691
00:47:20,700 --> 00:47:23,200
I made it especially for you.

692
00:47:24,166 --> 00:47:25,500
Go on, give it a try.

693
00:47:55,366 --> 00:47:56,691
Thitinant.

694
00:47:57,652 --> 00:47:59,835
If you've got pink eye,
go see a doctor.

695
00:48:00,694 --> 00:48:01,966
Don't go spreading it around here.

696
00:48:02,366 --> 00:48:03,735
Oh, come on, Boss!

697
00:48:04,190 --> 00:48:05,782
I was giving you a flirty look.

698
00:48:09,300 --> 00:48:10,007
Ugh!

699
00:48:11,574 --> 00:48:14,800
And what's wrong with your lips?
Why are they so pale?

700
00:48:18,700 --> 00:48:20,461
Well, it's the
'plain and wholesome' look, Boss.

701
00:48:20,461 --> 00:48:21,066
Ugh!

702
00:48:21,233 --> 00:48:23,400
went out of my way to do
my makeup just for you, Boss!

703
00:48:23,766 --> 00:48:25,000
And you don't even get it.

704
00:48:26,366 --> 00:48:28,566
If this is how you make up
to impress me,

705
00:48:29,600 --> 00:48:31,400
go back and try harder.

706
00:48:33,266 --> 00:48:36,400
And don't come slacking off
around here talking nonsense again.

707
00:48:37,233 --> 00:48:38,033
Get up.

708
00:48:44,700 --> 00:48:45,500
Understood.

709
00:48:49,066 --> 00:48:50,900
Don't forget to
drink your coffee, Boss.

710
00:48:51,566 --> 00:48:52,866
Maybe something sweet

711
00:48:53,566 --> 00:48:55,100
will put you in a better mood.

712
00:48:56,900 --> 00:48:58,833
Or did I not add enough sugar?

713
00:49:02,033 --> 00:49:04,000
But I guess sugar
isn't the problem, huh?

714
00:49:04,633 --> 00:49:06,300
It's probably your personality, Boss.

715
00:49:06,900 --> 00:49:07,700
Get out!

716
00:49:20,866 --> 00:49:22,233
Hello, Secretary Han.

717
00:49:22,700 --> 00:49:23,833
Order me a coffee, please.

718
00:49:25,100 --> 00:49:27,200
Make it extra bitter and strong.

719
00:49:33,557 --> 00:49:35,557
You little brat.

720
00:49:48,272 --> 00:49:50,509
(You barely eat or sleep,
and spend all your time working.)

721
00:49:50,509 --> 00:49:51,592
(No wonder you're so grumpy.)

722
00:49:51,592 --> 00:49:53,150
(When am I supposed to
find time to be with you?)

723
00:49:58,624 --> 00:50:00,624
(Overworking makes you look old, Boss!)
(Give your brain a break.)

724
00:50:01,170 --> 00:50:02,513
(Wow, you read that fast.
Were you waiting for my messages?)

725
00:50:02,513 --> 00:50:04,085
(You read but didn't reply?)

726
00:50:04,085 --> 00:50:06,011
(Let's see how long
you can stand being annoyed.)

727
00:50:12,460 --> 00:50:13,909
(If you have time to
send me this garbage,

728
00:50:13,909 --> 00:50:15,444
then make 50 copies
of the meeting minutes.)

729
00:50:15,444 --> 00:50:16,546
(And file them all before 4 PM.)

730
00:50:16,673 --> 00:50:18,828
(Boss, I saw how stressed you were,

731
00:50:18,828 --> 00:50:20,688
so I sent you some cuteness
to cheer you up.)

732
00:50:22,691 --> 00:50:23,869
(If I get another one of these
pointless messages,

733
00:50:23,869 --> 00:50:24,938
I'll deduct 500 baht
from your salary for each one.)

734
00:50:24,938 --> 00:50:26,385
(Starting with that last photo.)

735
00:50:26,385 --> 00:50:28,165
(Does this even count
as a nonsense text?)
(Better not risk it.
I don't want to get fined.)

736
00:50:35,200 --> 00:50:36,000
Ugh!

737
00:50:37,166 --> 00:50:39,166
Fifty sets of documents?

738
00:50:41,100 --> 00:50:42,866
You're really getting
your money's worth out of me.

739
00:50:44,500 --> 00:50:47,400
I should've asked
for triple the salary!

740
00:50:51,766 --> 00:50:52,600
Let's go home.

741
00:51:08,266 --> 00:51:09,066
Hey!

742
00:51:09,900 --> 00:51:10,700
Ouch!

743
00:51:12,433 --> 00:51:14,566
What's wrong with you now, old man?

744
00:51:27,300 --> 00:51:28,100
Ouch!

745
00:51:29,566 --> 00:51:31,233
Ow! I think my leg's broken!

746
00:51:31,966 --> 00:51:32,766
Ouch!

747
00:51:32,966 --> 00:51:33,800
I been hit by a car!

748
00:51:34,866 --> 00:51:35,577
I been hit by a car!

749
00:51:35,577 --> 00:51:36,269
Help!

750
00:51:36,269 --> 00:51:36,900
I been hit by a car!

751
00:51:37,600 --> 00:51:38,400
I been hit by a car!

752
00:51:39,866 --> 00:51:40,866
Oh, come on!

753
00:51:41,566 --> 00:51:42,633
I didn't even hit you.

754
00:51:43,266 --> 00:51:44,066
Wait a minute.

755
00:51:44,600 --> 00:51:45,400
I didn't hit you!

756
00:51:46,033 --> 00:51:47,200
I stopped in time.

757
00:51:47,466 --> 00:51:48,266
There was plenty of space between us.

758
00:51:49,400 --> 00:51:50,200
Oh.

759
00:51:50,366 --> 00:51:51,800
You were coming at me so fast.

760
00:51:52,066 --> 00:51:53,500
How was I supposed to dodge in time?

761
00:51:57,200 --> 00:51:58,966
Let me take a look.

762
00:52:00,066 --> 00:52:01,600
Easy, Boss!

763
00:52:02,100 --> 00:52:02,900
It hurts!

764
00:52:03,466 --> 00:52:04,266
Does it hurt here?

765
00:52:06,366 --> 00:52:07,166
Ow. It hurts.

766
00:52:07,666 --> 00:52:08,466
It hurts.

767
00:52:10,566 --> 00:52:11,500
Calm down.

768
00:52:12,266 --> 00:52:13,666
Okay, how about this? Um...

769
00:52:13,966 --> 00:52:15,700
I'll call an ambulance.

770
00:52:16,266 --> 00:52:17,633
About the expenses,

771
00:52:18,000 --> 00:52:19,634
I'll cover everything myself.

772
00:52:20,900 --> 00:52:22,066
I'm fine, Boss.

773
00:52:23,300 --> 00:52:24,466
There's no need to go that far.

774
00:52:31,033 --> 00:52:31,766
It hurts.

775
00:52:31,766 --> 00:52:32,566
Why?

776
00:52:33,766 --> 00:52:37,066
Or are you faking it?

777
00:52:38,800 --> 00:52:39,600
Oh, come on!

778
00:52:40,066 --> 00:52:42,000
Who would be crazy enough
to fake an injury?

779
00:52:45,033 --> 00:52:47,366
Then if you're fine, get up.

780
00:52:47,833 --> 00:52:50,266
Are you going to lie there
until another car runs you over?

781
00:52:50,900 --> 00:52:51,700
I'm leaving.

782
00:52:53,266 --> 00:52:54,833
Wait, Boss.

783
00:52:55,800 --> 00:52:58,100
Aren't you going to take
any responsibility for me?

784
00:52:59,500 --> 00:53:00,725
Responsibility for what?

785
00:53:00,927 --> 00:53:02,231
You're the one who jumped
in front of my car!

786
00:53:02,231 --> 00:53:04,602
There was plenty of distance
between us.

787
00:53:06,833 --> 00:53:07,818
Ouch!

788
00:53:17,523 --> 00:53:18,613
Calm down.

789
00:53:18,992 --> 00:53:20,133
Don't move yet.

790
00:53:21,460 --> 00:53:22,651
Just take it easy.

791
00:53:25,821 --> 00:53:27,409
Boss...

792
00:53:36,233 --> 00:53:37,800
If I can't walk anymore,

793
00:53:39,633 --> 00:53:42,166
you'll have to take care of me
for the rest of my life.

794
00:53:44,700 --> 00:53:45,766
I'll take responsibility,

795
00:53:46,433 --> 00:53:47,766
but not for the rest of your life.

796
00:53:49,366 --> 00:53:50,666
Can you walk?

797
00:53:51,900 --> 00:53:53,900
Come on. I'll help you.

798
00:53:56,000 --> 00:53:56,800
Boss...

799
00:53:57,566 --> 00:53:58,866
Am I going to die?

800
00:54:00,975 --> 00:54:02,077
You're not going to die.

801
00:54:02,077 --> 00:54:05,000
But you might need your leg amputated.

802
00:54:06,411 --> 00:54:07,956
No.

803
00:54:08,766 --> 00:54:09,566
Ouch!

804
00:54:09,700 --> 00:54:12,000
Stop making a scene
and get in the car. Let's go.

805
00:54:12,400 --> 00:54:13,600
I'll take you home.

806
00:54:23,000 --> 00:54:23,648
Ooh!

807
00:54:23,648 --> 00:54:24,148
Hey!

808
00:54:24,666 --> 00:54:25,766
It hurt my leg.

809
00:54:26,900 --> 00:54:28,490
I pushed your head,

810
00:54:28,490 --> 00:54:29,821
not your leg.

811
00:54:29,821 --> 00:54:30,766
Just a reminder.

812
00:54:38,321 --> 00:54:39,636
Oh!

813
00:54:39,636 --> 00:54:42,603
You were nice for five seconds,
then turned mean again.

814
00:54:47,833 --> 00:54:48,633
Boss...

815
00:54:48,766 --> 00:54:49,566
Hmm?

816
00:54:49,900 --> 00:54:51,266
Give me a hug, Boss.

817
00:54:53,966 --> 00:54:56,566
Your leg hurts,
and now your arms don't work either?

818
00:55:10,633 --> 00:55:13,887
If you're in this much pain,

819
00:55:13,887 --> 00:55:15,766
why don't you want to
go to the hospital?

820
00:55:17,200 --> 00:55:18,400
I can handle it.

821
00:55:21,500 --> 00:55:23,266
Just take me to my bed.

822
00:55:25,266 --> 00:55:27,000
I mean, my room is enough.

823
00:55:31,166 --> 00:55:31,966
Whatever you say.

824
00:55:36,833 --> 00:55:38,033
Go on, walk slowly then.

825
00:56:24,066 --> 00:56:25,366
How romantic.

826
00:56:53,256 --> 00:56:54,698
Are you live here?

827
00:56:55,104 --> 00:56:56,415
This place...

828
00:56:56,809 --> 00:56:58,317
Look kind of shady.

829
00:56:58,564 --> 00:57:00,000
I miss you, Nant.

830
00:57:00,310 --> 00:57:02,310
You blocked me on everything.

831
00:57:02,597 --> 00:57:04,597
If you run into someone
who's super stressed

832
00:57:05,179 --> 00:57:06,392
or unusually down,

833
00:57:06,392 --> 00:57:07,802
What can you do to
make them feel better?

834
00:57:08,122 --> 00:57:10,811
Ice cream is supposed to lower stress..

835
00:57:11,327 --> 00:57:14,262
but if I got to eat you whole, Boss,

836
00:57:15,663 --> 00:57:18,253
